{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>נאם. מקבץ נדחי ישראל.</b> [An utterance. He who gathers the outcasts of Israel.] For if [they] came up from Babylon and from Elam and Assyria:" "And the meaning of <b>לנקבציו</b> concerns the strangers, and behold, I will yet gather strangers upon the gathered ones of Israel, and the vav of לנקבציו reverts to Israel [i.e., the suffix refers back to Israel]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 56, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:48.911783631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}